      "authorization": "Root independently read the exact exception packet and supplied primary windows, and explicitly approved this exact challenger text. The premise amendment separately withdraws unsupported hidden-sector insensitivity and a paper-wide F-term-only assertion.",
      "originalText": "The illustrative K and W are additively separated. Parent context restricts the analysis to F-terms, treats hidden dynamics as insensitive to dark energy and requires a positive Kähler metric. Separation does not eliminate gravitational cou",
      "originalTextSha256": "ca798d67d5d3c220602a7f13faae74bf3a93dbd7be8614d464dd3e207c75bf91",
      "replacementText": "In the illustrative canonical supergravity model, K=|z|²+|Q|² and W=W0(z)+W1(Q) are additively separated, and the source evaluates the F-term scalar potential. The displayed canonical K gives a positive Kähler metric. Despite the separation, the potential contains the displayed contribution |W0|²|Q|²/M_Pl⁴, where M_Pl denotes the source's reduced Planck mass. Using the source's gravitino-mass relation, this contribution is of order m3/2²|Q|². Thus the example retains a hidden-sector contribution to the quintessence potential through supergravity. This qualification concerns the displayed calculation; it does not include an additional premise that hidden-sector dynamics are insensitive to dark energy, which the supplied windows do not establish.",
