      "authorization": "Root independently read the exact exception packet and supplied primary windows, and explicitly approved the challenger wording as an annotation-only refinement.",
      "originalText": "Supporting Kähler stabilization connects distinct inflaton sectors without identifying them. The card correctly leaves the chaotic inflaton unspecified and pr",
      "originalTextSha256": "27eb0b9f8c2ee1b9abaa0adbb17c01aba72819a412435be47b0d7e3ce027f543",
      "replacementText": "The supplied evidence supports retaining the compatibility question connecting distinct inflaton sectors through supporting Kähler stabilization. The d8 description leaves the chaotic inflaton's identity unspecified. The d11–d13 descriptions concern complex-structure or aligned-axion constructions, with negligible warping and explicitly included warping kept as separate settings. The d31 question concerns Kähler and five-brane moduli lacking membrane-instanton superpotentials and possible Fayet–Iliopoulos-driven five-brane inflation; its compactification framework is not inferred from the other sources. In e4 and e5, open-string radial motion drives the proposed α = 1/3 model in a type IIB/F-theory orbifold setup with intersecting D7 branes and near-conifold regions, while the closed-string sector is reported stabilized. The open-string contribution to τ3 and the convention ρ_k = b_k + iτ_k with b_k = 0 remain local to that setup. In e1 and e8, unwinding inflation uses a five-brane bubble in a warped Klebanov–Strassler throat within a type IIB Calabi–Yau orientifold compactification, with complex-structure moduli stabilized at tree level and two Kähler moduli stabilized through LVS. The specified backreaction analysis concerns anti-D3 charge effects on warping and changes in the scalar potential for the Kähler moduli as that charge is depleted. This does not establish control of every backreaction effect or resolve conjectural field-range bounds generally. The D7 analysis in e11 and e15 requires a suitable shift symmetry, nongeneric flux choices and preservation of extended no-scale loop suppression with an additional light D7 field; the shift symmetry is discussed near large complex structure. The authors report that they did not find an explicit flux in their stated example that preserves the desired light brane sector while stabilizing the axio-dilaton and all complex-structure moduli. This limitation is not a nonexistence theorem. These are source-specific compatibility questions and reported constructions, not interchangeable brane mechanisms or independently verified compactifications.",
