      "authorization": "Root independently read the exact exception packet and supplied primary windows, and explicitly approved the challenger wording as an annotation-only refinement.",
      "originalText": "The broad geometric question is useful with its existing boundaries: transforming only K changes the specified construction, positive-energy rolling is not au",
      "originalTextSha256": "05b8698c74cb1d242ae4073a8216865f0f76fb7de91b47c20d66465981cc84fc",
      "replacementText": "The supplied evidence supports retaining the broad geometric question with its existing source-specific boundaries. In d18, a field transformation is applied only to the Kähler potential while a prescribed holomorphic superpotential is retained; equivalence under a simultaneous transformation of the full theory is not established by that description. The d15 question concerns positive-energy rolling of the real part of a Kähler modulus after axion displacement from a supersymmetric vacuum, while remaining in that vacuum's effective theory; it does not itself establish slow-roll inflation. The d21 question assumes that a saxion is absent from the leading Kähler-potential term, not that the saxion is absent from the theory; this condition remains local to that asymptotic question. The Hubble-to-gravitino comparison in d1 and the seven-disk targets 3α = 1,…,7 in d14 remain description-level questions. Separately, e4 and e5 report an α = 1/3 open-string pole-inflation construction in a type IIB/F-theory orbifold setup with intersecting D7 branes and near-conifold regions. Its open-string moduli are associated with D3 branes. The authors assume that the near-conifold region arises from warping of the largest four-cycle, τ3, and that the open-string moduli contribute only to τ3. The convention ρ_k = b_k + iτ_k, with b_k set to zero for simplicity, remains local to that construction. The two α-attractor routes are not identified by their numerical overlap. The setting facets o15 and o34 add no independent primary evidence, and the supplied windows do not establish a general classification or a global embedding for every geometric construction.",
